    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d167">

                <pb facs="0395" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.0144/49</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Russian
                        Affairs, Department of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Poole</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The attached memorandum was handed to me today by the Russian Ambassador.<anchor
                        n="9" xml:id="d167-f1"/> He said that he thought that Wrangell Island had no
                    political or economic importance and that it should not become in any way the
                    subject of controversy. He only wished to put on record his point of view with
                    respect to the matter inasmuch as it has received so much publicity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. C. Poole</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d167-a1.xml" xpointer="d167-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d167-f1" n="9" xml:id="d167-f1-content">
                <p>Boris Bakhmeteff, Russian Ambassador since July 5, 1917.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
